RIGIDITY = witness orbit dimension; sub-orbit structure (cyclic units vs doubling)
  n=7: AP witness clock-points = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]  (= units (Z/n)*? True); |orbit|=phi(n)=6
       under DOUBLING x2 mod n, the unit witnesses split into orbits: [[1, 2, 4], [3, 6, 5]]
  n=8: AP witness clock-points = [1, 3, 5, 7]  (= units (Z/n)*? True); |orbit|=phi(n)=4
       under DOUBLING x2 mod n, the unit witnesses split into orbits: [[1], [3], [5], [7]]
  n=12: AP witness clock-points = [1, 5, 7, 11]  (= units (Z/n)*? True); |orbit|=phi(n)=4
       under DOUBLING x2 mod n, the unit witnesses split into orbits: [[1], [5], [7], [11]]
  n=14: AP witness clock-points = [1, 3, 5, 9, 11, 13]  (= units (Z/n)*? True); |orbit|=phi(n)=6
       under DOUBLING x2 mod n, the unit witnesses split into orbits: [[1], [3], [5], [9], [11], [13]]
  n=16: AP witness clock-points = [1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13, 15]  (= units (Z/n)*? True); |orbit|=phi(n)=8
       under DOUBLING x2 mod n, the unit witnesses split into orbits: [[1], [3], [5], [7], [9], [11], [13], [15]]

Flexible (loose) example -> positive-measure witness (dim 1):
  V=(1, 4, 5) (n=4): safe-measure=0.0750 -> FLEXIBLE(dim1)
  V=(2, 3, 7, 8) (n=5): safe-measure=0.1071 -> FLEXIBLE(dim1)
